# ── Dependencies ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/

# ── Build output ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# dist/ is regenerated by `npm run build`, which is what Vercel runs on every
# deploy. Committing a 107 MB artifact that is derived from the source it sits
# next to would only create a second thing that can disagree with the first.
dist/
*.local

# ── Generated by the verification probes ──────────────────────────────────────
# scripts/theme-audit.mjs writes screenshots here for eyeballing. They are
# outputs, not inputs, and they change on every run.
.theme-audit/
*-probe-*.png

# ── Python venv ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Only used for offline sanity-checks of the ONNX model. The app needs no Python.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ── Vercel ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Holds the project + org IDs that link this checkout to a Vercel project. It is
# machine-local: another clone links itself with `vercel link`.
.vercel/

# ── Secrets ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The app has no backend and no server-side key, so nothing here should ever be
# needed. Listed anyway, because the cost of being wrong once is permanent —
# a key pushed to a public repo is compromised even after it is deleted.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# ── Third-party reference material ────────────────────────────────────────────
# A saved copy of the Perchance image-generator page, kept locally while wiring
# up that integration. It is someone else's page: not ours to redistribute, and
# not referenced by any code.
pc.html

# ── Editor / OS noise ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
*.swp
*~

# ── Logs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# ── Deliberately NOT ignored ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# public/models/  — the bundled Pix2Text ONNX weights (~58 MB, largest file
#                   ~22 MB, so well inside GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit).
#                   Offline OCR is the app's main claim; a clone without these
#                   would silently lose it, and the whole point is that a fresh
#                   `git clone && npm i && npm run build` produces the real app.
# public/ort/     — same reasoning for the onnxruntime-web WASM binaries.

.vercel
.env*
